  "worked_solution": "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(x-5)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot (x+3) \\\\  & =-3x+15-2x-6 \\\\  & =-5x+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ -5x & =-9 \\\\ x & =\\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
